# Cipher — E2E Messaging Architecture

iPhone-only E2E encrypted messenger. Server relays ciphertext only; it must never hold decryption keys or perform encrypt/decrypt.

## Stack

| Layer | Choice |
|-------|--------|
| Client | Xcode, Swift, SwiftUI |
| Crypto | Signal Protocol library + CryptoKit; private keys in Keychain |
| Local DB | SQLite / SwiftData |
| Backend | Go on Ubuntu (Docker), PostgreSQL, Redis, Nginx |
| Hosting | VPS preferred (Hetzner / OVH / DigitalOcean) |
| Push | APNs (no sensitive content in payloads) |
| Transport | HTTPS/TLS + certificate pinning |

## Non-negotiables

- Do **not** invent cryptography; use Signal Protocol (or MLS later for groups if chosen).
- All encrypt/decrypt happens on device; server stores/forwards ciphertext blobs only.
- Encrypt attachments before upload; server stores ciphertext.
- Auth: invite codes only (small friend circle — no email/phone login) → session token later.
- Store: encrypted blobs, sender/recipient IDs, timestamps, delivery status, public keys, push tokens — never plaintext messages.

## Client responsibilities

Generate keys, encrypt/decrypt, verify identities (QR / safety numbers), store chats locally.

## Security features to prefer

Face ID/Touch ID app lock, Keychain keys, device verification, key rotation, disappearing messages, remote session revocation. Optional: screenshot/jailbreak detection.

## Later / optional

Voice/video: WebRTC + DTLS-SRTP. Groups: Signal group messaging (or MLS).

